<h1>Hardware Settings - Calibration and Alignment Tab</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Calibration and Alignment</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">Tab displays the settings concerning the alignment and calibration.</span></p>
<p><img src="../images/calibration_and_alignment.gif" width="551px" height="485px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">Calibration and alignment section</p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Calibration filename</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Displays the currently used calibration and alignment files.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Calibration file has the same name as sensor's serial number and the extension is <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>.mcl</b></span>. The old <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>3cl</b></span> format can still be used if the file extension is renamed from <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>.3cl</b></span> to <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>.mcl</b></span>. A copy of the calibration file can be made using <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Copy to disk</b></span> button.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Alignment filename</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">User can select different alignment files: use <span class="Button">Browse</span> button. Their extension is <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>.alf.</b></span></p>
<p class="whs5"><img src="../images/Select_Alignment.gif" width="321px" height="199px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Press <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Select</b></span> button to select existing alignment file or <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Make new alignment</b></span> button to start the Alignment wizard in order to perform new alignment.</p>
<p class="Warning">Every time the localiser is changed KUBE issues a warning and unloads the current alignment file.</p>
<p>When all changes are made, confirm with <span class="Button">Apply</span> button.</p>

